window.message:
fix(ef6): Build/BuildAsync seed the database once per creator (#734)

The classic EF6 DbContextBuilder<T> re-ran the whole seed on every
Build()/BuildAsync() call on one builder, re-adding the same instances to
the same Effort database. Mirror the EF Core builder's #559 fix:

- remember the creator whose database has been seeded (_seededCreator);
  later builds on it return a context without seeding again;
- a new creator (UseEffort) is a new, empty database and is seeded again;
- every SeedWith/SeedWithRandom overload throws InvalidOperationException
  after the first build on the current cre

